WEBVTT

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.440
<i>Generator...</i>

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:11.410
<i>...X-Drive!</i>

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.480
This is...

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.700
...the shape of a miracle.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.390
<b>Episode 13 
Believe in Justice, and Hold It Close</b>

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.430
Are you okay?

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.210
Tears?

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:03.620
One on six...

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.710
She's an alchemist.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:09.050
There's no point in counting the numbers!

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:11.800
And we've got the X-Drive to finish her.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.760
It's over!

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:19.340
You think simply wielding a 
miracle will defeat me?

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.560
We all created this power together!

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.890
You think the word "miracle" can describe it?

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.140
Of course!

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:27.930
A miracle...

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:34.100
When my father saved the village from a plague,

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:38.080
the foolish villagers called his work a miracle.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.450
And then they burned him at the stake

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.790
because they said he had no right to create one.

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:46.620
Your father?

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.960
Lifting the veil over reality's fundamental principles

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:55.760
and recording them in the 
Château de Tiffauges was my task.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.930
In other words, completing the 
Apocalypse of All Things.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.850
But...

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.510
Carol-chan is crying?

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:08.750
Miracles are a plague, no different than 
the one that struck my village!

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.410
That's why I swore I would destroy them...

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:16.570
That's why I refuse to lose to 
someone wielding a miracle!

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.500
What is she trying to do?

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.630
Carol still has...

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.840
...so many Alca-Noise?

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.330
Even without the Château de Tiffauges,

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:42.010
she has enough to destroy the world?

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:45.140
Right now, all we can do...

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:48.850
Hibiki...

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:50.140
Hibiki!

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.650
That voice... Dad?

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:56.280
Hibiki, a child is crying here!

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:04.910
If a child is crying, you have to reach out
 your hand to them, right?

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:08.200
If I just destroy everything!

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.130
Tsubasa-san!

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:21.090
I know, Tachibana.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:25.080
It isn't my first time doing this with you screwballs.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:30.010
We'll split up and destroy

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:32.140
the Alca-Noise individually!

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:39.900
<i>Souls entrusted.</i>

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.530
<i>Souls connected.</i>

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:46.490
<i>She's just like us.</i>

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:49.780
<i>A light takes flight to the heavens,</i>

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.240
<i>She was oppressed, downtrodden.</i>

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:55.250
<i>drawn on the string of a bow.</i>

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.150
<i>But she kept struggling, trying to change things.</i>

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:57.410
<i>The only difference is that she was alone!</i>

00:03:57.110 --> 00:04:02.510
<i>Bringing together a billion loves,</i>

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.130
<i>I have to save her.</i>

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:07.460
<i>we bring together time.</i>

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.850
<i>Because I was saved, too.</i>

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:12.600
<i>Now we return to the song of the heartbeat</i>

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:10.400
<i>And to do that,</i>

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:15.060
<i>I shall wield a miracle and rise 
as many times as I must!</i>

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:18.400
<i>that began everything.</i>

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.230
<i>And so,</i>

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:20.560
<i>we'll sing a song in this warring sky!</i>

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:25.930
<i>Souls creating.</i>

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:30.700
<i>Held in arms.</i>

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:35.710
<i>Strong like the Sun.</i>

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:41.090
<i>Kind like the Moon.</i>

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:46.550
<i>The future suddenly appears.</i>

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:52.810
<i>The story moves to its ending.</i>

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:59.060
<i>And it will bloom again.</i>

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:05.850
<i>A miracle will soon become history,</i>

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:11.750
<i>shining and proud!</i>

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:10.760
The power of the X-Drive...

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:15.080
However, Carol's phonic gain is just as strong.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:24.930
Those Alca-Noise were just an attempt to buy time?

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:28.260
She plans to burn every last memory she has?

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.800
If I simply destroy everything...

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.430
The world, miracles,

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:36.600
and my memories!

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:44.150
I swore I'd save her!

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.830
That's right! Come with me, Maria!

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:58.120
Begone!

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:00.480
Senpai!

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:01.290
Maria!

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:07.920
What is that?

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.470
<i>I'll return everything to the void.</i>

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:30.860
<i>I don't even think I care anymore.</i>

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:35.370
<i>But if I don't do it, the ache 
beneath my belly won't stop.</i>

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.830
She's attacking!

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:50.350
That power... How strong has she become?

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:52.360
Then we'll just get her...

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:53.600
...before she gets us!

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:54.180
Hey!

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.550
Her defenses are impregnable.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:05.400
Unless we focus our fire, we won't break through!

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:11.320
Then we'll gather our X-Drive energy into 
our Armed Gears, and push through!

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:16.780
It's a big risk, but that's our most powerful attack.

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:19.370
And we can use it together!

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:22.080
Talk later! There's more coming!

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.920
Quick! While I'm blocking it!

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.100
Let's do it!

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:53.180
You were one Armed Gear short...

00:07:58.050 --> 00:08:00.930
I'll destroy miracles! All the miracles!

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:03.750
I'll become a murderer of miracles!

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.170
Tachibana!

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:23.440
This hand, which connects with others,
 is my Armed Gear!

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.750
<i>If this fist connects, it hurts.</i>

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:31.550
<i>But Miku taught me that it can 
do more than only hurt!</i>

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:35.160
I'll flatten you like a pillow.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.580
A rejection? Now?

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.260
No...

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:47.810
These memories of Papa are trying to stop me!

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:53.030
I refuse to accept that... I refuse!

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:55.780
I don't need memories that will defy me!

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:58.640
I'll burn them all and turn them into power!

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.280
Lend our power to Tachibana...

00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:23.450
Ame no Habakiri!

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:24.700
Ichaival!

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:25.960
Shul Shagana!

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.210
Igalima!

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:28.710
Airgetlám!

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:42.380
Gungnir!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.650
The energy's lost its outlet 
and is going out of control!

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:07.500
Estimating damage now.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:10.880
Sixty seconds until the energy reaches criticality!

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:14.110
The surrounding twelve kilometers 
will be caught in the explosion,

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:17.310
and any buildings within three kilometers 
will be badly damaged!

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:20.760
It's like a miniature sun.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:25.180
I'll show you a truth you will never forget...

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:28.140
That, in this world, songs can't save anything.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.560
I won't give up.

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:31.770
If I have to, I'll draw in a miracle!

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:33.660
Miracles are curses.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:35.940
They kill those who cling to them.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:37.150
Twenty seconds!

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:41.980
Carol-chan!

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.540
Take my hand!

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:52.310
Your songs can't save me.

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:54.650
They can't save anyone!

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:56.210
I'll save you, anyway.

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:57.460
<i>Drawn Blade!</i>

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:59.300
<i>Dáinsleif!</i>

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.050
Carol!

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:08.140
Carol... Know more of the world.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:09.180
Papa!

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:12.180
The task we've been given is to ensure that,

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:14.810
someday, people can understand one another.

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:18.430
You're smart, so you know this, right?

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:20.980
And you know what you have to do.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.820
Papa!

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:46.110
I see.

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:49.110
Then no one knows where Carol is yet?

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:53.030
It's been seventy-two hours 
since the battle ended.

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:55.060
I don't know if there's any point in continuing.

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:56.250
Understood.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:58.880
Call off the search and return.

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:00.140
Roger.

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:03.600
Since Hibiki-chan was safe when we found her,

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:06.130
she's probably alive.

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:10.450
I'm concerned about more than 
just the missing Carol.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:13.960
I'm glad you came.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.460
I'm sorry to make you come every day.

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:19.330
It's summer vacation now, so it's okay!

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:21.400
Summer vacation?

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:24.080
Summer vacation is great.

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:25.800
It's our first one, too!

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:28.100
You don't have to get up early,

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:29.860
and you can stay up as late as you want!

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:32.590
That's just your lifestyle, Hibiki.

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:35.270
Don't give her any weird ideas!

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:38.900
During summer vacation, 
the shopping street holds a festival!

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:42.720
Yakisoba, cotton candy, takoyaki, and grilled squid!

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:46.030
Between you and me, when she gets excited,

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:48.780
Maria-san's Gear plays a Bon Odori song.

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.130
Is that true?

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:54.240
Of course not!

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:58.290
That would sound better coming from 
Tsubasa's Gear than mine.

00:13:03.020 --> 00:13:05.030
I see. I see.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:07.240
I understand exactly what

00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:10.560
you all think of the Ame no Habakiri...

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:15.020
There's so much I don't know yet, isn't there?

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:20.240
If I can learn more about 
the world, about all of you,

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:23.900
could I be closer to you than I am now?

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:25.410
You can!

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:30.620
So you have to get better soon, right?

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:42.270
Okay, see you tomorrow.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:44.170
Get well soon!

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:49.050
I'm going to the bathroom...

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:51.850
Very well.

00:13:56.930 --> 00:13:57.910
Let's go.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:00.840
We aren't waiting for her to come back?

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:01.650
It's fine.

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:21.540
I'm sorry...

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:24.160
If I cry,

00:14:24.560 --> 00:14:28.560
Elfnein-chan won't get better when 
she's supposed to, right?

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:41.600
The only problems you can solve with your fists

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:44.500
are the easy ones...

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:49.580
The only things I can do are so small.

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:53.640
It's really frustrating.

00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:58.340
Maybe.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:00.670
But you know...

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:05.760
When you're doing what you think is right,

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:07.600
your clenched fist is special.

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:10.300
Special?

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:13.920
It's the gentlest fist in the world.

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:17.600
Someday, I'm sure it will

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:20.060
fix all of the bad things.

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:22.450
Miku...

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:31.030
Thank you.

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:33.530
You really are

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:36.130
my sunflower.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:10.320
Carol...

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:12.440
Carol.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:15.250
That's my name.

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:19.390
Amnesia...

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:24.620
Because you burned most of your memories.

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:27.370
They're in pieces.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:31.130
And hazy, like a fog is covering them.

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:35.500
Who am I?

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:40.540
When I close my eyes, I see you.

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:44.460
So I thought you might know, and I came here.

00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:46.570
You are

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:49.520
the other me.

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:54.040
I'm the other you?

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:55.530
Yes...

00:16:56.280 --> 00:17:01.410
The two of us followed the 
words that Papa left us.

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:04.540
Papa's words...

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:07.520
I forgot something

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:09.670
so important?

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:11.660
Tell me...

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:15.330
Even as we speak, I'm...

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:19.850
You...

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:26.310
I'll start from the beginning...

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:30.160
I can't share it in a few words

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:33.340
because my body is like this.

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:35.720
You're almost gone, as well,

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.570
just like I am?

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:46.690
Yes.

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:51.280
I thought I was fine with that,

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:53.900
as long as I could save the world...

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:00.350
But...

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:04.680
Right now, I don't want to disappear!

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:08.190
In that case,

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:10.790
the two of us can do it again.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:45.720
Carol-chan?

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:57.160
I am...

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:35.170
I shouldn't have any good memories of this town.

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:37.980
But right now, it feels like I do.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.270
Isn't that because you've

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:43.150
gotten stronger than you once were?

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:46.490
I'll have to

00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:49.550
do my best, too. Right?

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:52.080
Yeah, Dad!

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:54.250
It's all right! Everything's just fine!

00:19:56.930 --> 00:19:59.950
What happened to our fun summer vacation?

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:03.500
Why doesn't Chris-senpai seem worried?

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:05.850
This is a good chance to tell you something.

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:07.440
I may not look it,

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:10.600
but I get pretty good grades.

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:11.840
No way!

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:15.440
I-It was Shirabe who said that!

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:18.820
What happened to the Kiri-chan who 
was supposed to protect me?

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:21.070
Finish your damned homework!

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:27.500
Tsubasa-san...

00:20:31.760 --> 00:20:34.670
You know, I also go to England once in a while.

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:37.330
Once in a while, huh?

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:43.050
That sword isn't feminine, after all.

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:47.680
Don't you think you're a failure as a father,

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:50.180
not being able to see her off?

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:53.220
This is enough for us...

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:54.950
More importantly, Gen,

00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:58.690
what's your take on this Magical Girl Incident?

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:04.390
Since the US fell from power, 
trouble has been brewing in Europe.

00:21:04.810 --> 00:21:06.250
Or perhaps...

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:10.450
I'm sorry I'm late!

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:12.020
You really are.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:14.320
I'm sorry.

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:18.420
Let's get back to our analysis.

00:22:57.010 --> 00:23:02.190
I want to start over with everyone, 
one more time, so...

00:23:19.490 --> 00:23:21.750
I guess you wouldn't just take my hand—

00:23:25.690 --> 00:23:26.950
Hibiki...

00:23:29.410 --> 00:23:33.650
I'm holding your hands because
 I believe it's the right thing to do.

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:35.510
So...

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:39.280
I won't let go of them easily!

00:23:46.400 --> 00:23:50.030
<b>Fin</b>
